> Docs\SITE_SEAT_V2.md:5:> Later on October 21: Level 1 (`Docs/LEVEL1.md`, K29 to K36) comes first. Its hub is full 
passthrough with one panel and three crew buttons, and the warp moves the site rather than the rig. The table model, 
PM standee, stake markers and wrist panel described here return in later levels.
  Docs\SITE_SEAT_V2.md:6:
  Docs\SITE_SEAT_V2.md:7:## What the test found
  Docs\SITE_SEAT_V2.md:8:
  Docs\SITE_SEAT_V2.md:9:1. The player fell through the world at start, so the start panel seemed to fly up. Likely 
cause, to verify: the Interactions Rig block brings Interaction SDK locomotion (the scene contains its locomotor with 
a gravity factor), and nothing under the player has a collider.
  Docs\SITE_SEAT_V2.md:10:2. Our scripts built or copied the rig, the passthrough layer and a controller pointer 
(`XRSceneSetup`, `ControllerPointer`) instead of relying on Meta's Building Blocks, which have proven more reliable in 
Bryan's projects.
  Docs\SITE_SEAT_V2.md:11:3. The seat was VR only. In a three-person game in one room, the headset player must see and 
talk with the other two.
  Docs\SITE_SEAT_V2.md:12:
> Docs\SITE_SEAT_V2.md:13:## XR setup rules (Building Blocks only)
  Docs\SITE_SEAT_V2.md:14:
  Docs\SITE_SEAT_V2.md:15:1. The XR rig in `Site.unity` is made of Building Blocks that Bryan adds in the Editor: 
Camera Rig, Passthrough, Controller Tracking, Interactions Rig (which brings Hand Tracking) and Real Hands. They are 
in the scene as of October 21. Grab Interaction and Teleport are not needed now.
  Docs\SITE_SEAT_V2.md:16:2. No code creates, copies, parents or reconfigures a camera rig, a passthrough layer, or 
controller or hand objects. Runtime code finds them by component (`OVRCameraRig`, `OVRPassthroughLayer`, the 
Interaction SDK interactors) and reads their anchors.
  Docs\SITE_SEAT_V2.md:17:3. Pointing, pressing and selecting go through the Interaction SDK interactors that the 
Interactions Rig provides, for controllers and hands alike: ray at a distance, poke for buttons within reach. Our 
objects become interactable with Interaction SDK components (`RayInteractable` with a collider surface, 
`PokeInteractable`, `PointableCanvas` for uGUI panels) and react through its pointer events. No raycasts on `OVRInput`.
> Docs\SITE_SEAT_V2.md:18:4. No locomotion and no gravity. `LOB Over > Setup > Configure Building Blocks` switches off 
the Interactions Rig's locomotion (teleport, slide, turn, the locomotor and its gravity) and sets the tracking origin 
to floor level. A floor collider at the tracked floor height exists in the hub and in the site regardless. The only 
way to move is the warp.
  Docs\SITE_SEAT_V2.md:19:5. The scene belongs to Bryan. The builder edits only the objects it owns, whose root names 
start with `[LOBOver]`, inside the existing `Site.unity`. It never replaces the scene and never touches 
`[BuildingBlock]` objects, `OVRCameraRig`, or anything else it did not create. Demo objects that came with blocks 
(`[BuildingBlock] Cube`, `Poke Interaction`) are switched off, not deleted, and listed for Bryan.
  Docs\SITE_SEAT_V2.md:20:6. `LOB Over > Setup > Check Building Blocks` reports each required block as present or 
missing and stops any build that lacks one, naming the block to add from the Building Blocks window.
  Docs\SITE_SEAT_V2.md:21:
  Docs\SITE_SEAT_V2.md:22:## The experience
  Docs\SITE_SEAT_V2.md:23:
  Docs\SITE_SEAT_V2.md:24:1. **Hub, in passthrough.** The player stands in the real room and sees the team, the Plan 
laptop and the paper. On the table, 0.6 m ahead at 0.75 m height (a wrist button re-places it), is the site as a 2 m 
model: trench states, water, crews and machines moving, zone boards, the sky. A PM standee at the model's near corner 
uses LOB-Game's PM portraits: `explaining` for the morning brief and while a PM line plays, `worriedSurprise` for a 
few seconds when an event card arrives, `clipboard` otherwise. It never shows `thumbsUp` or `crossedArms`, which 
LOB-Game uses as outcome reactions and which would read as verdicts here. The model shows only what the full-scale 
site shows: no plan, no money, no forecast numbers. In a solo demo for stakeholders the Plan panel may float above it; 
never in a team game.
> Docs\SITE_SEAT_V2.md:25:2. **Warp in.** Point at a stake, a crew or a zone board on the model and select. The warp 
takes about 1.2 s: a ring of light opens at the player's feet, the site replaces the room from the ground outward 
through a noise-edged dissolve with a bright edge, and the player stands at that stake at full scale, facing the 
trench. The player does not travel; the world changes around them, so there is no vection. Real Hands keeps the 
player's own hands visible. The simulation receives `moveTo` for that station and `dismount` on arrival.
> Docs\SITE_SEAT_V2.md:26:3. **In the site, in VR.** Look at a thing for two seconds to inspect it, or point at it and 
select. The wrist panel on the left hand or controller has Flag, Stop work, Confirm (Done or Not carried out) and Back 
to table, pressed by poke or ray. Foremen speak from where they stand. Stake markers along the trench warp to another 
stake with a short version of the effect (0.6 s). There is no truck.
> Docs\SITE_SEAT_V2.md:27:4. **Warp out.** Back to table plays the dissolve in reverse; the room returns, and the 
model marks where the player was.
  Docs\SITE_SEAT_V2.md:28:5. **Cards and prompts.** Event cards (facts only) float above the model in the hub and 
appear on the wrist panel in the site. Guide prompts (guided mode, `Docs/PLAYTHROUGH.md`) appear in the same places 
with a Ready button.
  Docs\SITE_SEAT_V2.md:29:
  Docs\SITE_SEAT_V2.md:30:## Two modes
  Docs\SITE_SEAT_V2.md:31:
  Docs\SITE_SEAT_V2.md:32:1. **Team game.** The headset is the Site seat of a game hosted by the Node host on the PC. 
The world is drawn from the host's `state` messages and every verb goes to the host. Over USB, run `adb reverse 
tcp:7331 tcp:7331` on the PC and use host address `127.0.0.1` (no Wi-Fi needed); wirelessly, use the PC's LAN address. 
Plan plays on `plan.html`, Rules on `rules.html` or the printed kit, the facilitator on `facilitator.html`.
  Docs\SITE_SEAT_V2.md:33:2. **Solo demo.** The embedded C# simulation with Plan on autopilot, as built in WO-S3 and 
WO-S4, for one person or a stakeholder audience.
  Docs\SITE_SEAT_V2.md:34:
> Docs\SITE_SEAT_V2.md:35:## The warp effect, technically
  Docs\SITE_SEAT_V2.md:36:
  Docs\SITE_SEAT_V2.md:37:An alpha-write dissolve over the eye buffer, with passthrough as the underlay: passthrough 
shows wherever the eye buffer's alpha is 0, the same principle as Meta's selective passthrough. An inward-facing 
sphere around the head, drawn after everything else, writes alpha from a threshold on the radial distance from the 
player's feet plus noise, and writes an emissive colour in a thin band at the edge. It must support single-pass 
instanced stereo and hold 72 Hz on the Quest 3S. Parameters: duration, edge width, edge colour, noise scale. If the 
shader cannot run, the fallback is a 0.3 s fade through black.
  Docs\SITE_SEAT_V2.md:38:
> Docs\SITE_SEAT_V2.md:39:## Comfort rules
  Docs\SITE_SEAT_V2.md:40:
  Docs\SITE_SEAT_V2.md:41:1. No camera motion the player did not make with their head.
> Docs\SITE_SEAT_V2.md:42:2. A warp never exceeds 1.2 s, and the player can look around during it.
  Docs\SITE_SEAT_V2.md:43:3. The hub is the rest frame; Back to table ends a VR stint at any time.
> Docs\SITE_SEAT_V2.md:44:4. Nothing follows the head except the warp sphere during a warp.
  Docs\SITE_SEAT_V2.md:45:
  Docs\SITE_SEAT_V2.md:46:## For stakeholders
  Docs\SITE_SEAT_V2.md:47:
> Docs\SITE_SEAT_V2.md:48:Cast the headset to a laptop or TV through the Meta Horizon app or Meta's casting page, so 
the room sees the warp and the site while the headset player talks with Plan and Rules.
using System;
using System.Collections;
using System.IO;
using System.Linq;
using LOBOver.Sim;
using Newtonsoft.Json;
using Newtonsoft.Json.Linq;
using UnityEngine;
using Simulation = LOBOver.Sim.Sim;

namespace LOBOver.Runtime
{
    public sealed class Director : MonoBehaviour
    {
        public string scenarioId = "slice_texas";
        public SiteView SiteView { get; private set; }
        public PlanView PlanView { get; private set; }
        public JObject Job { get; private set; }
        public JObject MachineCatalog { get; private set; }
        public JArray Lines { get; private set; }
        public double DeadlineDay { get; private set; }
        public double TimeDays => simulation == null ? 0 : simulation.T;
        // Same day boundary as Common.DisplayDay; view snapshots use simulation time instead.
        public int DisplayDay => (int)Math.Floor(TimeDays + 1e-6) + 1;
        public string Speed => simulation == null ? "paused" : simulation.Speed;
        public bool Ready => simulation != null;
        public bool Done => simulation != null && simulation.Done;
        // WO-S4 Amendment 1: pausing the script leaves its cursor untouched.
        private bool autoplanEnabled = true;
        public bool AutoplanEnabled
        {
            get => autoplanEnabled;
            set
            {
                if (autoplanEnabled == value) return;
                autoplanEnabled = value;
                if (value && simulation != null && autoplan != null)
                { autoplan.Advance(simulation.T, Apply); Publish(); }
            }
        }
        public double ScenarioSecondsPerDay => secondsFull;
        public double SecondsPerDay
        {
            get => playbackSeconds ?? secondsFull;
            set
            {
                if (double.IsNaN(value) || double.IsInfinity(value) || value <= 0)
                    throw new ArgumentOutOfRangeException(nameof(value));
                playbackSeconds = value;
            }
        }
        public string LoadError { get; private set; }
        public string TranscriptPath { get; private set; }
        public event Action Loaded;
        public event Action<SiteView, PlanView> ViewsChanged;
        public event Action<JObject> Message;
        public event Action<JObject> Event;
        public event Action<JObject> Voice;
        public event Action<JObject> Result;

        private Simulation simulation;
        private Scenario scenario;
        private Catalog catalog;
        private Autoplan autoplan;
        private Pacer pacer;
        private Coroutine loading;
        private double secondsFull, secondsSlow;
        private double? playbackSeconds;
        private JObject transcript;
        private JArray snapshots, messages, commands;
        private int lastSnapshot = -1;
        private bool savedResult;

        private void OnEnable() { if (!Ready && loading == null) Load(scenarioId); }

        // Public Start is also Unity's lifecycle method. A slow Android load is started by OnEnable.
        public void Start()
        {
            if (simulation == null || simulation.Done) return;
            Apply("facilitator", new JObject { ["action"] = "start" });
            Publish();
        }
        public void Pause()
        {
            if (simulation == null) return;
            Apply("facilitator", new JObject { ["action"] = "pause" });
            Publish(); SaveTranscript();
        }
        public void Reset()
        {
            if (scenario == null) return;
            SaveTranscript(); Initialize();
        }
        public void Load(string id)
        {
            if (id != "slice_texas" && id != "stage1_texas" && id != "stage2_texas")
                throw new ArgumentException("Unknown scenario: " + id, nameof(id));
            SaveTranscript();
            if (loading != null) StopCoroutine(loading);
            pacer?.Close(); simulation = null; SiteView = null; PlanView = null;
            scenarioId = id; LoadError = null;
            playbackSeconds = null;
            loading = StartCoroutine(LoadFiles());
        }
        private IEnumerator LoadFiles()
        {
            // Let scene subscribers attach before File-backed Editor reads can finish.
            yield return null;
            string catalogText = null, scenarioText = null, scriptText = null;
            Action<string> failed = error => { LoadError = error; Debug.LogError(error, this); };
            yield return StreamingData.ReadText("Data/catalog.json", value => catalogText = value, failed);
            if (LoadError != null) yield break;
            yield return StreamingData.ReadText("Data/Scenarios/" + scenarioId + ".json", value => scenarioText = value, failed);
            if (LoadError != null) yield break;
            var script = scenarioId == "slice_texas" ? "slice_autoplan" : scenarioId == "stage1_texas" ? "stage1_pm_play" : "stage2_pull_play";
            yield return StreamingData.ReadText("Data/scripts/" + script + ".json", value => scriptText = value, failed);
            if (LoadError != null) yield break;
            try
            {
                var source = JObject.Parse(scenarioText);
                catalog = Catalog.Load(catalogText); scenario = Scenario.Load(scenarioText, catalog);
                Job = (JObject)source["job"].DeepClone();
                MachineCatalog = (JObject)JObject.Parse(catalogText)["machines"];
                Lines = (JArray)source["lines"].DeepClone();
                DeadlineDay = (double)source["plan"]["deadlineDay"];
                secondsFull = (double)source["time"]["secondsPerDayFull"];
                secondsSlow = (double)source["time"]["secondsPerDaySlow"];
                if (secondsFull <= 0 || secondsSlow <= 0) throw new InvalidDataException("Scenario day lengths must be positive");
                // Autoplan removes Site entries; the presenter retains every Site verb.
                autoplan = new Autoplan(JArray.Parse(scriptText));
                Initialize();
            }
            catch (Exception error) { failed(error.ToString()); }
            loading = null;
        }
        private void Initialize()
        {
            pacer?.Close(); simulation = Simulation.Create(scenario, catalog); autoplan.Reset();
            snapshots = new JArray(); messages = new JArray(); commands = new JArray();
            transcript = new JObject { ["scenario"] = scenarioId, ["snapshots"] = snapshots,
                ["messages"] = messages, ["commands"] = commands, ["result"] = null };
            TranscriptPath = Path.Combine(Application.persistentDataPath, "transcripts",
                scenarioId + "-" + DateTime.UtcNow.ToString("yyyyMMdd-HHmmss-fff") + ".json");
            lastSnapshot = -1; savedResult = false;
            pacer = new Pacer(() => simulation, AfterTick);
            Loaded?.Invoke();
            if (AutoplanEnabled) autoplan.Advance(simulation.T, Apply);
            Start();
            Drain(); CaptureDay();
        }
        private void Update()
        {
            if (simulation == null) return;
            // Pacer's 5/20-second day cadence is scaled to the scenario's full/slow seconds per day.
            var baselineMs = (Speed == "slow" ? Pacer.SLOW_MS : Pacer.FULL_MS) / Pacer.STEP_DAYS;
            var authoredMs = (Speed == "slow" ? secondsSlow : secondsFull) * 1000;
            // Preserve the authored full/slow ratio when the presenter changes playback speed.
            if (playbackSeconds.HasValue) authoredMs *= playbackSeconds.Value / secondsFull;
            pacer.Advance(UnityEngine.Time.unscaledDeltaTime * 1000 * baselineMs / authoredMs);
            Publish();
        }
        private void AfterTick()
        {
            if (AutoplanEnabled) autoplan.Advance(simulation.T, Apply);
            Drain(); CaptureDay();
            if (simulation.Done && !savedResult) { savedResult = true; SaveTranscript(); }
        }
        private void Apply(string seat, JObject command)
        {
            var reply = simulation.Apply(seat, command);
            commands.Add(new JObject { ["t"] = simulation.T, ["seat"] = seat, ["cmd"] = command.DeepClone() });
            var acknowledgement = JObject.FromObject(reply);
            acknowledgement["t"] = reply.Ok ? "ack" : "nack";
            acknowledgement["id"] = command["id"];
            messages.Add(new JObject { ["t"] = simulation.T, ["message"] = acknowledgement });
            // Only the initiating seat receives its rejection text.
            if (seat == "site") Message?.Invoke(acknowledgement);
            Drain();
        }
        public void Send(JObject command)
        {
            if (simulation == null || command == null) return;
            Apply("site", command); Publish();
        }
        // presenter-only (MR diorama); the full-scale seat and the JavaScript sim do not have it
        public JObject InspectAt(string target, double stationFt) => simulation?.InspectAt(target, stationFt);
        public static bool ForSeat(JObject message, string seat) =>
            message["seats"] is JArray seats && seats.Any(value => (string)value == seat);
        private void Drain()
        {
            foreach (var message in simulation.Drain())
            {
                messages.Add(new JObject { ["t"] = message["day"] ?? new JValue(simulation.T), ["message"] = message.DeepClone() });
                Message?.Invoke(message);
                if ((string)message["t"] == "event") Event?.Invoke(message);
                if ((string)message["t"] == "voice") Voice?.Invoke(message);
                if ((string)message["t"] == "result") Result?.Invoke(message);
            }
        }
        private void Publish()
        {
            SiteView = SiteView.From(simulation.View("site"));
            PlanView = PlanView.From(simulation.View("plan"));
            ViewsChanged?.Invoke(SiteView, PlanView);
        }
        private void CaptureDay()
        {
            var day = (int)Math.Floor(simulation.T + 1e-6);
            if (day == lastSnapshot) return;
            snapshots.Add(simulation.View("facilitator")); lastSnapshot = day;
            SaveTranscript();
        }
        public void SaveTranscript()
        {
            if (transcript == null || simulation == null) return;
            transcript["result"] = simulation.Result;
            try
            {
                Directory.CreateDirectory(Path.GetDirectoryName(TranscriptPath));
                File.WriteAllText(TranscriptPath, transcript.ToString(Formatting.Indented));
            }
            catch (IOException error) { Debug.LogWarning("Transcript: " + error.Message, this); }
            catch (UnauthorizedAccessException error) { Debug.LogWarning("Transcript: " + error.Message, this); }
        }
        private void OnApplicationPause(bool paused) { if (paused) SaveTranscript(); }
        private void OnDisable()
        {
            SaveTranscript();
            if (loading != null) { StopCoroutine(loading); loading = null; }
        }
        private void OnDestroy() { pacer?.Close(); }
    }
}
using System;
using System.Collections;
using System.IO;
using UnityEngine;
using UnityEngine.Networking;

namespace LOBOver.Runtime
{
    public static class StreamingData
    {
        public static string Url(string relative)
        {
            var path = Application.streamingAssetsPath.TrimEnd('/') + "/" + relative;
            return path.Contains("://") ? path : new Uri(path).AbsoluteUri;
        }

        public static IEnumerator ReadText(string relative, Action<string> loaded, Action<string> failed)
        {
#if UNITY_ANDROID && !UNITY_EDITOR
            using (var request = UnityWebRequest.Get(Url(relative)))
            {
                yield return request.SendWebRequest();
                if (request.result == UnityWebRequest.Result.Success) loaded(request.downloadHandler.text);
                else failed(relative + ": " + request.error);
            }
#else
            string value;
            try { value = File.ReadAllText(Path.Combine(Application.streamingAssetsPath, relative)); }
            catch (Exception error) { failed(relative + ": " + error.Message); yield break; }
            loaded(value);
            yield break;
#endif
        }
    }
}
